{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06J1", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:47eae5b4bf0155beb30eb5aeccbdc300b70340dec4d41e329036f9b3da456dc9", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nFinally we define the notion of a deformation category.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ede2926301ef3562f1a9149a10e55fbf1b53ba803923a3d0d201d7dbdf8aede9", "unit_id": "tag:06J1:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06J1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-deformation-category}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dd5c28dbd5934d4de7f5cc67c3b95dd19e3e63b51b3b2c2b1f3c713c1475afd6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:329a67876e95e884bac3f7f5d98545c9d3f58ef59e2a6205b72d3490e0a09a1e", "source_text": "A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>deformation category<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a predeformation category <MATH_0001>\nsatisfying (RS). A morphism of deformation categories is a morphism of\ncategories over <MATH_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:999ca98e97f42a3bbd651008cd7ba445786e0ec0ed5254d8f9366f11f0af287a", "unit_id": "tag:06J9:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "06J1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F: \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$F(k)$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\overline{\\mathcal{F}}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-RS-associated-functor}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-deformation-functor}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:91ecf16eff38be66c7a7d0267f15907774e9296ddd297e5016130e8353dbf578", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ca5e505fc4a1551d4070c172ccc0c713b82eb3ffc57d22ce3a6c435d66f9a8bf", "source_text": "We say that a functor <MATH_0001>\nis a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>deformation functor<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if the associated cofibered set is a\ndeformation category, i.e.<SPACE_0001>if <MATH_0002> is a one element set and <MATH_0003> satisfies\n(RS). If <MATH_0004> is a deformation category, then\n<MATH_0005>\nis a predeformation functor but not necessarily a deformation functor, as\nLemma <REF_0001> shows.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aa2880a77ad5924756fa212c1eecc8d0b3c9ad61305d9f7ae90a2b78828a9e00", "unit_id": "tag:06JA:statement"}
